{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And You have given us.</b> The matter turns on the לֹא said above — meaning, You have not brought us, and You have not given us an inheritance of field and vineyard. You said to us: ״אַעֲלֶה אֶתְכֶם מֵעֳנִי מִצְרַיִם אֶל אֶרֶץ טוֹבָה״ (Exodus 3) — from there You took us out, and not to a land flowing with milk and honey have You brought us; rather, You decreed upon us to die in the wilderness, for You said to us: ״בַּמִּדְבָּר הַזֶּה יִפְּלוּ פִגְרֵיכֶם״ (Numbers 14)." "<b>Will the eyes of those men be gouged out, etc.</b> Even if You send to gouge out our eyes if we do not come up to You — we will not come up." "<b>Those men.</b> Like a person who hangs his curse on his fellow."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:17.700258843Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}